BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:breakfast-msp@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261124T130616Z
DTSTART:20261204T071500Z
DTEND:20261204T080000Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Coffee session: Connecting long-term energy scenarios wit
 h marine spatial planning
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Marine spatial planning (MSP) determines how marine space is us
 ed and is a key enabler of accelerated\, responsible offshore wind deploym
 ent – a growing part of many long-term energy scenarios. This session ex
 amines how energy planners and marine spatial planners can work together s
 o that each process informs the other\, using more granular MSP data to im
 prove forecasts of timelines and infrastructure needs\, with a focus on in
 stitutional coordination and data governance.\n\nProvisional programme\, c
 heck for changes: https://energyplanningweek.info/#breakfast-msp
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#breakfast-msp
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:deep-dive-1@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261124T130616Z
DTSTART:20261204T080000Z
DTEND:20261204T090000Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Deep Dive 1: Greening data centres – principles for sou
 nd energy planning under uncertainty
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:AI and data centres are driving rapid growth in electricity dem
 and. Poorly planned\, this new demand can strain networks and raise emissi
 ons\; well-designed procurement and siting can instead accelerate addition
 al renewables\, flexibility and grid investment. Building on IRENA's work 
 on green data centres\, this session explores how principles for credible 
 renewable electricity supply can be linked with system and infrastructure 
 planning to address anticipated data centre demand despite prevailing unce
 rtainty.\n\nProvisional programme\, check for changes: https://energyplann
 ingweek.info/#deep-dive-1
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#deep-dive-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:deep-dive-2@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261124T130616Z
DTSTART:20261204T090000Z
DTEND:20261204T100000Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Deep Dive 2: Robust power system planning – linking gri
 d infrastructure and flexibility
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:As solar and wind shares grow and electrification reshapes dema
 nd\, power systems need more grid capacity and more flexibility\, and the 
 two are closely linked. This session shares experiences in connecting nati
 onal energy scenarios with grid and flexibility planning: where grid expan
 sion is needed\, where flexibility offers a cost-effective complement\, an
 d how to avoid unnecessary investment while maintaining reliability.\n\nPr
 ovisional programme\, check for changes: https://energyplanningweek.info/#
 deep-dive-2
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#deep-dive-2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:deep-dive-3@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261124T130616Z
DTSTART:20261204T103000Z
DTEND:20261204T120000Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Deep Dive 3: Regional energy planning – aligning nation
 al priorities and regional interconnection
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Regional institutions and planning entities from different worl
 d regions share how national plans inform regional transmission developmen
 t and vice versa\, the institutional mechanisms that support coordination\
 , and the challenges that remain.\n\nProvisional programme\, check for cha
 nges: https://energyplanningweek.info/#deep-dive-3
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#deep-dive-3
END:VEVENT
